{# Why Local Matters #}
<section class="why-local">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="why-local-grid">
      <div class="why-local-content">
        <p class="section-eyebrow">Local Expertise</p>
        <h2>Why Local Matters for Gutters</h2>
        
        <p>North Alabama presents unique challenges for gutter systems. Our 20+ years serving this region means we understand:</p>
        
        <ul class="checkmarks">
          <li>✓ <strong>Red Clay Soil</strong> — North Alabama's clay doesn't absorb water, making proper drainage critical</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Heavy Rainfall</strong> — 55+ inches annually demands properly sized gutters and downspouts</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Pine Needle Season</strong> — Our solutions prevent clogging from year-round pine needle drop</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Spring Storm Season</strong> — Fast response when severe weather damages your gutters</li>
          <li>✓ <strong>Summer Humidity</strong> — We use materials that resist the rust and rot our climate accelerates</li>
        </ul>
        
        <p>When you choose Blue River Gutters, you're choosing a team that knows your neighborhood, responds quickly, and stands behind their work.</p>
        
